## Project Structure

```plaintext
src/
├── components/
├── pages/
├── layouts/
├── hooks/
├── services/
├── utils/
├── constants/
├── context/
├── assets/
├── types/
├── routes/
├── styles/
├── App.tsx
└── main.tsx
```

---

## Folder Breakdown

### components/

Reusable UI components used throughout the application.

Contains:

- Buttons
- Cards
- Inputs
- Modals
- Tables
- Status badges
- Navigation components
- Analytics widgets

Purpose:

Ensures interface consistency and reusable design logic.

---

### pages/

Application screens and route-level views.

Includes:

- Landing Page
- Login
- Signup
- Dashboard
- Invoice Builder
- Invoice Management
- Receipt Generator
- Client Vault
- Reports
- Settings

Purpose:

Represents the full product workflow.

---

### layouts/

Shared layout structures.

Includes:

- Dashboard layout
- Authentication layout
- Mobile navigation layout

Purpose:

Maintains structural consistency.

---

### hooks/

Custom reusable application logic.

Examples:

- useAuth
- useInvoice
- useClientData
- useTheme

Purpose:

Encapsulates reusable business logic.

---

### services/

Handles core product operations.

Includes:

- Authentication services
- Invoice generation
- PDF export
- Receipt conversion
- Analytics processing

Purpose:

Separates business logic from UI rendering.

---

### utils/

Helper functions.

Examples:

- Currency formatting
- Date formatting
- Invoice calculations
- Validation logic

Purpose:

Improves maintainability.

---

### constants/

Stores reusable static configuration.

Examples:

- Status definitions
- Currency options
- Navigation items
- Theme variables

Purpose:

Centralized configuration management.

---

### context/

Global application state management.

Includes:

- User context
- Theme context
- Invoice state
- Client state

Purpose:

Supports scalable state flow.

---

### assets/

Static design assets.

Includes:

- Logos
- Icons
- Illustrations
- Brand imagery

Purpose:

Visual resource management.

---

### types/

TypeScript type definitions.

Examples:

- Invoice types
- Client interfaces
- User schemas

Purpose:

Improves type safety.

---

### routes/

Application route definitions.

Purpose:

Controls page navigation structure.

---

### styles/

Global styling files.

Includes:

- Global CSS
- Theme tokens
- Utility classes

Purpose:

Maintains design system consistency.

---

### App.tsx

Main application routing and structure orchestration.

---

### main.tsx

Application entry point.

Responsible for:

- Rendering root application
- Mounting providers
- Initial setup

---
```
